   "conventions": [
    "The paper uses \u27e8H_i\u27e9 = v_i/\u221a2 with v = 246 GeV, the same as ADROIT's normalisation. ADROIT's v = 246.22 GeV is used in the formulas.",
    "The paper's hypercharge convention matches Q = T3 + Y (doublets have Y = 1/2); no halving was needed.",
    "V enters L as \u2212V: the portal V_port = iB a0 H1\u2020H2 + h.c. becomes L \u2283 \u2212iB a0 H1\u2020H2 + h.c.",
    "Rotation to the Higgs basis: H = c\u03b2 H1 + s\u03b2 H2 and \u03a6 = \u2212s\u03b2 H1 + c\u03b2 H2. Under it H1\u2020H2 \u2192 H\u2020\u03a6 c\u03b2\u00b2 \u2212 \u03a6\u2020H s\u03b2\u00b2 + (H\u2020H \u2212 \u03a6\u2020\u03a6) s\u03b2c\u03b2. The real parts cancel against their h.c., leaving i B a0 H\u2020\u03a6 + h.c.",
    "Physical inputs are converted to Lagrangian parameters. B = (m_A\u00b2 \u2212 m_a\u00b2) sin2\u03b8/(2v). m_A0\u00b2 = c\u00b2\u03b8 m_A\u00b2 + s\u00b2\u03b8 m_a\u00b2 and m_a0\u00b2 = s\u00b2\u03b8 m_A\u00b2 + c\u00b2\u03b8 m_a\u00b2. Here c\u00b2\u03b8 and s\u00b2\u03b8 = (1 \u00b1 sqrt(1 \u2212 sin\u00b22\u03b8))/2.",
    "Type II Yukawas are rewritten in the Higgs basis with Y_d c\u03b2 = \u221a2 m_d/v and Y_u s\u03b2 = \u221a2 m_u/v. This gives a \u03a6 coupling of +tan\u03b2 for d-type quarks and leptons, and \u2212cot\u03b2 for up-type quarks via \u03a6\u0303. The SM Yukawas to H are left to G1.",
    "\u03a6's neutral imaginary component equals \u2212A0 in the paper's notation, an overall sign that does not affect the spectrum."
   ],
